<title>USA: Pentagon expects fighter jet announcement Nov 18.</title>
<headline>Pentagon expects fighter jet announcement Nov 18.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pentagon expects to announce on Nov 18 the two final bidders in a contest to build next-generation strike fighter aircraft for the U.S. military and U.K. Royal Navy, a Defense Department spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The market-sensitive news is planned for late afternoon.</p>
<p>Three bidders are vying for the contract to build about 3,000 &quot;joint strike fighter&quot; jets. They include Boeing Co, Lockheed Martin Corp, and a joint bid by McDonnell Douglas Corp, Northrop Grumman Corp and British Aerospace Plc. The two finalists will have 3-1/2 years to build prototypes, with a winner chosen in 2001.</p>
</text>
